      "id": "find-remapped-field-9b7d34",
      "name": "FindRemappedField",
      "category": "MemberReference",
      "signature": "FindRemappedField(Field Class, Initial Scope, Initial Name, Initial Scope Must Be Owner Of Field For Parent Scope Redirect)",
      "params": [
        {
          "name": "Field Class",
          "type": "UClass*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Initial Scope",
          "type": "UClass*"
        },
        {
          "name": "Initial Name",
          "type": "Name"
        },
        {
          "name": "Initial Scope Must Be Owner Of Field For Parent Scope Redirect",
          "type": "Bool",
          "default": "false"
        }
      ],
      "returnType": "UField*",
      "docs": "Searches the field redirect map for the specified named field in the scope, and returns the remapped field if found\n@param\tFieldClass\t\tUClass of field type we are looking for\n@param\tInitialScope\tThe scope the field was initially defined in.  The function will search up into parent scopes to attempt to find remappings\n@param\tInitialName\t\tThe name of the field to attempt to find a redirector for\n@param\tbInitialScopeMustBeOwnerOfFieldForParentScopeRedirect If true, and a redirect is found in a parent scope, and the targetscope of the redirect\nis a child scope of the parent scope that is not the initial scope or a parent of the initial scope, then the redirect will be ignored.\n@return\tThe remapped field, if one exists"
    },
